# Deep Fix — Hydration Mismatches (Logo + Typewriter)

## Context
Two persistent hydration errors after page load:

1. **Navbar logo `<img>`** — Next.js `<Image>` with SVG + `priority` + inline `style={{ width: 'auto', height: 'auto' }}` produces different inline `style` on SSR vs CSR. Server emits `height: auto`, client drops it. This is a Next 16.2.3 + Turbopack quirk specific to SVG + Image style merging.
   - File: [src/components/layout/navbar.tsx:551-559](src/components/layout/navbar.tsx#L551-L559)

2. **Typewriter** — even after gating motion behind a `mounted` flag, the SSR HTML keeps emitting the static branch (className-only span) while the CSR first-paint emits the motion branch (inline-styled `<span>` + nested `motion.span`). The `useReducedMotion` hook from framer-motion + React 19 hydration timing is causing the post-mount commit to overwrite the hydration boundary before React detects mismatch. The mounted-flag pattern is not strong enough.
   - File: [src/components/home/typewriter.tsx](src/components/home/typewriter.tsx)
   - Used by: [src/components/home/hero.tsx:34](src/components/home/hero.tsx#L34)

Goal: eliminate **both** hydration mismatches with no behavior regression. Logo must render identical bytes SSR + CSR. Typewriter must show the first phrase ("Ownership Driven") as plain text on first paint (SSR) and animate phrase changes only after client mount.

## Files to Modify
1. [src/components/layout/navbar.tsx](src/components/layout/navbar.tsx) — swap `<Image>` SVG logo to plain `<img>`
2. [src/components/home/typewriter.tsx](src/components/home/typewriter.tsx) — split into SSR-safe shell + client-only animated cycler
3. [src/components/home/hero.tsx](src/components/home/hero.tsx) — no source change needed; consumer of `<Typewriter />` stays intact

## Change 1 — Logo: drop Next/Image for SVG
Next/Image gives no benefit for SVG (no resize, no AVIF/WebP, no LCP optimization). Its style merging is the root cause of the diff. Replace with plain `<img>`:

```tsx
{/* navbar.tsx:551 — replace the existing <Image> block */}
<img
  src="/images/webflow/Group-46895.svg"
  alt="Boldteq logo"
  width={130}
  height={40}
  className={styles["logo"]}
  decoding="async"
/>
```

Drop `next/image` import if no longer used elsewhere in this file (verify with grep). Drop the inline `style={{ width: 'auto', height: 'auto' }}` — `.logo` CSS module already handles sizing via `width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: contain` on the parent `.nav-23-logo`.

## Change 2 — Typewriter: client-only motion via `next/dynamic` with `ssr: false`
Split the component into two files:

**A. New `src/components/home/typewriter-motion.tsx`** — moves the motion-driven cycler. This is the file that contains `framer-motion` imports and runs the phrase-cycling interval:

```tsx
'use client';

import { AnimatePresence, motion, useReducedMotion } from 'framer-motion';
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import styles from './hero.module.css';

const PHRASES = ['Ownership Driven', 'Without Hiring', 'On Demand'] as const;

export default function TypewriterMotion() {
  const [index, setIndex] = useState(0);
  const prefersReducedMotion = useReducedMotion();

  useEffect(() => {
    if (prefersReducedMotion) return;
    const id = setInterval(() => {
      setIndex((p) => (p + 1) % PHRASES.length);
    }, 2400);
    return () => clearInterval(id);
  }, [prefersReducedMotion]);

  if (prefersReducedMotion) {
    return (
      <span className={`${styles['animate-span']} ${styles['typewriterContainer']}`}>
        {PHRASES[index]}
      </span>
    );
  }

  return (
    <span
      aria-live="polite"
      aria-atomic="true"
      className={styles['typewriterContainer']}
    >
      <AnimatePresence mode="wait">
        <motion.span
          key={index}
          className={`${styles['animate-span']} ${styles['typewriterWord']}`}
          initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 10 }}
          animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
          exit={{ opacity: 0, y: -10 }}
          transition={{ duration: 0.28, ease: 'easeInOut' }}
        >
          {PHRASES[index]}
        </motion.span>
      </AnimatePresence>
    </span>
  );
}
```

**B. Rewrite `src/components/home/typewriter.tsx`** — exports a stable SSR shell + dynamically loads the motion variant client-only:

```tsx
'use client';

import dynamic from 'next/dynamic';
import styles from './hero.module.css';

const FIRST_PHRASE = 'Ownership Driven';

// Client-only motion variant — never rendered on the server, so it cannot mismatch.
// Fallback emits the exact same DOM the SSR shell renders, so layout doesn't shift on hydration.
const TypewriterMotion = dynamic(() => import('./typewriter-motion'), {
  ssr: false,
  loading: () => (
    <span className={`${styles['animate-span']} ${styles['typewriterContainer']}`}>
      {FIRST_PHRASE}
    </span>
  ),
});

export function Typewriter() {
  return <TypewriterMotion />;
}
```

Why this works:
- SSR + first client paint render the `loading` fallback, which is a single span with the first phrase as plain text — zero motion, zero conditional branches, zero `useReducedMotion` calls. Bytes match.
- After hydration, Next.js client loader swaps in `TypewriterMotion`, which mounts cleanly because it never participated in hydration.
- The fallback uses the exact same `className` as the post-mount static branch, so layout (`min-width: 280px`, etc.) stays stable across the swap — no CLS.

## Change 3 — Hero consumer
[hero.tsx:34](src/components/home/hero.tsx#L34) keeps `<Typewriter />` import + usage unchanged. No edit needed.

## Out of Scope
- Other Next/Image usages (raster images benefit from optimization — keep them).
- PortfolioCarousel `column-4x-large-centered` and BenefitsGrid `<a>` vs `<div>` warnings shown in the prior log were Turbopack stale-cache artifacts; they self-resolve on dev restart. No source changes there.
- Footer changes already shipped earlier in this session (white input bg).

## Verification
1. Stop dev server, clear cache:
   ```bash
   rm -rf .next && pnpm dev
   ```
2. Open `http://localhost:3000`
3. Browser DevTools → Console: zero hydration warnings on first load + on full reload.
4. View source (`Cmd+U`) → confirm:
   - Navbar `<img src="/images/webflow/Group-46895.svg" width="130" height="40" class="...logo">` (no inline style attribute, no `data-nimg`)
   - Hero typewriter span has `Ownership Driven` as plain text in the SSR HTML
5. After hydration, watch the typewriter cycle through "Ownership Driven" → "Without Hiring" → "On Demand" every 2.4s.
6. macOS System Settings → Accessibility → Display → enable "Reduce motion", reload — verify text stays static (no interval) and no console warnings.
7. Lighthouse run: confirm CLS ≤ 0.05 on the hero (no layout shift when motion variant swaps in).

